{
  "id": "exponential-and-logarithmic-functions",
  "title": "Exponential and Logarithmic Functions",
  "term": 1,
  "summary": "The definition of a logarithm, the logarithm laws, solving exponential equations with logarithms, and the graphs of $y = b^x$ and $y = \\log_b x$.",
  "notes": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "What is a logarithm?"
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "latex": "y = \\log_b x \\iff x = b^y \\qquad (b > 0,\\ b \\neq 1,\\ x > 0)",
      "caption": "A logarithm is an exponent: $\\log_b x$ is the power to which $b$ must be raised to give $x$"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate (a) $\\log_2 32$ (b) $\\log_3 \\frac{1}{9}$ (c) $\\log 1\\ 000$",
      "steps": [
        "(a) $2^5 = 32$, so $\\log_2 32 = 5$",
        "(b) $3^{-2} = \\frac{1}{9}$, so $-2$",
        "(c) $\\log$ without a base means base 10: $10^3 = 1\\ 000$, so $3$"
      ],
      "answer": "(a) 5 (b) −2 (c) 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Logarithm laws"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Law",
        "Example"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "$\\log_b (xy) = \\log_b x + \\log_b y$",
          "$\\log 2 + \\log 5 = \\log 10 = 1$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\log_b \\dfrac{x}{y} = \\log_b x - \\log_b y$",
          "$\\log_3 18 - \\log_3 2 = \\log_3 9 = 2$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\log_b x^n = n\\log_b x$",
          "$\\log_2 8^5 = 5\\log_2 8 = 15$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\log_b b = 1$ and $\\log_b 1 = 0$",
          "$\\log_7 7 = 1$"
        ],
        [
          "Change of base: $\\log_b x = \\dfrac{\\log x}{\\log b}$",
          "$\\log_2 10 = \\dfrac{1}{\\log 2} \\approx 3{,}32$"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Solving exponential equations"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 2",
      "problem": "Solve for $x$, correct to two decimal places: $5^{x} = 40$",
      "steps": [
        "Take logs: $x = \\log_5 40 = \\dfrac{\\log 40}{\\log 5}$",
        "$x \\approx 2{,}29$"
      ],
      "answer": "$x \\approx 2{,}29$"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 3: finance application",
      "problem": "How long will it take R2 000 to grow to R5 000 at 9% p.a. compounded annually?",
      "steps": [
        "$5\\ 000 = 2\\ 000(1{,}09)^n$, so $(1{,}09)^n = 2{,}5$",
        "$n = \\dfrac{\\log 2{,}5}{\\log 1{,}09} \\approx 10{,}63$",
        "It takes about 11 years (10,63 years)."
      ],
      "answer": "About 10,63 years"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Graphs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "$y = \\log_b x$ is the reflection of $y = b^x$ in $y = x$.",
        "Domain of $y = \\log_b x$: $x > 0$. Range: $y \\in \\mathbb{R}$.",
        "Both pass through a fixed point: $y = b^x$ through $(0; 1)$, $y = \\log_b x$ through $(1; 0)$.",
        "If $b > 1$, $\\log_b x$ is increasing; if $0 < b < 1$, it is decreasing."
      ]
    },
